L3afpad @VERSION@ - a simple text editor (GTK 3) for RISC OS

L3afpad 0.8.18.1.11 by Tarot Osuji and Steven Honeyman (GPL version 2),
on GTK 3 through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: the first real GTK program
in the riscos-gtk project.

Using it
- Run it, or drop a text file on !L3afpad in a Filer window.
- Click Menu over the window for its menu (File, Edit, Search, Options,
  Help). Keyboard short-cuts are shown in the menus (^S save, ^O open...).
- Drag a text file from a Filer window onto the window to open it.
- File > Save As: a RISC OS Save box. Drag its icon to a Filer window, or
  give a full name and click Save. Names without an extension are saved
  as Text (&FFF).
- File > Open: an Open box. Drag a file to it from a Filer window.
- File > New empties the window (asking to save first): RISC OS runs one
  copy of a program, so there's no second window.
- Text in UTF-8 and other encodings is detected when opening; RISC OS's
  Latin-1 is read through the Iconv module.

Not yet
- Printing (GTK has no printing on RISC OS yet).
- Double-clicking a text file doesn't open it here (no icon bar icon yet).

Messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.L3afpad.Log. Please send it, with a note of
anything that behaves differently from a RISC OS editor.

